## How we work

**Open Claude Code sessions HERE — at this trunk-checkout root** (never inside
a `$HOME/wt/...` campaign worktree — auto-memory is keyed by the directory a
session opens in, so worktree-anchored sessions fragment and orphan project
memory). Campaign work is driven from this anchor: cd into the worktree within
the session, or use `git -C <worktree>`.

Concurrent sessions at this anchor are normal — but **the anchor's own tree
takes writes from ONE session at a time** (git staging is shared: another
session's `commit` can sweep up your staged files, and its post-merge
`reset --hard` wipes your uncommitted edits). Trunk writes — docs commits,
merges, resets — belong to the coordinator lane; every other session treats
the anchor as read-only and drives only its own worktree. Memory hygiene for
parallel sessions: re-read `MEMORY.md` from disk right before adding an index
line (your session-start copy may be stale) and add it as a one-line edit,
never a full-file rewrite; re-read a memory file from disk before basing a
load-bearing decision on it.

Working discipline lives in the ohd plugin (way-of-working ·
campaign-land · campaign-status · claude-md-sanity); lifecycle tooling is
`tools/campaign.sh`. Sessions without the plugin: see the plugin repo's
`docs/campaign-dropin.md`.

